{"seq":2,"slug":"pathology-microbiology","title":"第二章 动物病理与微生物学","docCount":3,"url":"/l-doc-books/education/university/agriculture/veterinary/pathology-microbiology","docs":[{"seq":1,"slug":"pathology-basics","title":"大学兽医学 — 病理学基本概念","url":"/l-doc-books/education/university/agriculture/veterinary/pathology-microbiology/pathology-basics","wordCount":1792,"readingTime":8},{"seq":2,"slug":"pathogens","title":"大学兽医学 — 病原微生物与寄生虫","url":"/l-doc-books/education/university/agriculture/veterinary/pathology-microbiology/pathogens","wordCount":1769,"readingTime":8},{"seq":3,"slug":"immunology-vaccines","title":"大学兽医学 — 免疫系统与疫苗","url":"/l-doc-books/education/university/agriculture/veterinary/pathology-microbiology/immunology-vaccines","wordCount":1932,"readingTime":8}],"introHtml":"<h1 id=\"第二章-动物病理与微生物学\">第二章 动物病理与微生物学</h1><p>如果说第一章描述的是&quot;健康的样子&quot;，本章则探讨&quot;为什么会生病&quot;。病理学研究疾病状态下细胞、组织和器官发生的结构与功能改变，微生物学则聚焦致病的细菌、病毒、寄生虫等&quot;敌人&quot;本身。</p>\n<p>本章先建立病理学的基本概念（炎症、坏死、肿瘤等通用损伤模式），再系统认识各类病原微生物的特性与致病机制，最后讲解免疫系统这套&quot;防御部队&quot;如何识别和清除入侵者，以及疫苗为何能保护动物群体。</p>\n"}